In a recent conversation, James Rising received an email from Ariquzzaman Tiash, a prospective PhD student with a background in Public Policy and Environmental Economics. Tiash expressed interest in joining James's research group and provided a brief overview of his qualifications, including work on the Social Cost of Carbon. James asked for assistance in drafting a professional response, which highlighted that he currently has no available spaces and advised Tiash to check back at the end of 2026. The final email also included an invitation for Tiash to schedule a Zoom chat to discuss his interests further.
